Context (pp. 62-64). Let S be a base with 2 invertible, Sigma_J = P^1_S, and J = {0,1,infty} with an extra section t of P^1 - J (so t, t-1 are units). The four points I_t = J ∪ {t} are the images of the 2-torsion of a Legendre-type elliptic curve E_0 under the Kummer quotient p: E_0 -> E_0/{±1} = P^1. Here the origin is sent to t, not to infinity. The Klein four-group V of 2-torsion translations descends to a group of involutions of P^1 permuting I_t. Multiplication by 2 descends to a degree-4 self-map f_2^t of P^1 (a Lattès map). Grothendieck wants to characterise this map using only J and t, as on p. 62, (32)-(33).

Step 1, formula (34). For each i in J, sigma_i^t is the unique involution of P^1 swapping t with i and swapping the other two points of J:
- sigma_0^t(z) = (z-t)/(z-1);
- sigma_1^t(z) = t/z;
- sigma_infty^t(z) = t(z-1)/(z-t);
- and sigma_infty^t = sigma_0^t sigma_1^t, so together with the identity they form a Klein four-group.
All of this checks.

Step 2, formula (35). Delta_i^t is the fixed-point scheme of sigma_i^t, an étale double cover of S:
- Delta_0^t: z^2 - 2z + t = 0;
- Delta_1^t: z^2 - t = 0;
- Delta_infty^t: z^2 - 2tz + t = 0.
The fixed points of translation by a 2-torsion point T on the Kummer line are the images of the P with P + T = -P, i.e. 2P = T. Hence f_2^t(Delta_i^t) = i, which is (36).

Step 3. Degree 4 with all six critical points known determines f up to a unit:
 f_2^t = c_t ((z^2 - 2z + t)/(z^2 - 2tz + t))^2.
To find c_t, evaluate at zeta with zeta^2 = t:
- the numerator becomes 2(t - zeta) and the denominator 2t(1 - zeta);
- (t - zeta)/(1 - zeta) = -zeta;
- so f(zeta) = c_t/t, and imposing the value 1 gives c_t = t.
The next page then checks that f(I_t) = t and that iterates give the 2^n maps, with f^{-n}(t) = p(E_0[2^n]).

Conceptual content, implicit in the construction. f_2^t is invariant under V, since [2] kills the 2-torsion translations. It is therefore exactly the quotient map P^1 -> P^1/V ≅ P^1. Its six critical points are the Delta's and its three critical values are 0, 1, infty. So for each t it is the degree-4 'Klein four' Belyi-type cover with ramification (2,2)^3. The free V-orbit I_t goes to the point t, so its post-critical set is {0,1,infty,t}. This is a description of the Lattès map of the Legendre family over Z[1/2]-schemes, using only the four marked points.
